  "title": "India's Cash Paradox and Economic Challenges",
  "summary": "India's cash circulation and digital payments show a paradox, with the country continuing to struggle with liquidity amid rising crude oil prices and geopolitical tensions, while the RBI's liquidity mop-up efforts aim to stabilize the rupee and address economic challenges.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) absorbed Rs 1.91 trillion through liquidity mop-up auctions, increasing demand for liquidity amid surplus reserves.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "India's trade deficit widened to $31.98 billion in Q1FY27, partially offset by growth in exports of petroleum products, electronics, engineering, and marine goods.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
